<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 15 June, from 763 BCE to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">763 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,788 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bur-Sagale eclipse is seen in Assyria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A total solar eclipse was recorded in Assyrian eponym lists, most likely in the tenth year of King Ashur-dan III. It is the earliest solar eclipse mentioned in historical sources that has been successfully identified.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/923">923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert I of West Francia is killed at Soissons</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Robert I fell in battle against the deposed Carolingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a>, though his side won the field. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a> later founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-dynasty">Capetian dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1215">1215 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">811 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King John agrees to Magna Carta at Runnymede</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing rebel barons, John accepted a charter limiting royal power and promising justice under law. Though soon annulled, it was reissued and became a lasting symbol of constitutional government.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1219">1219 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">807 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Valdemar II of Denmark wins the Battle of Lindanise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crusading army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> of Rävala at Lindanise, the site of present-day Tallinn, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> claimed northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>. Legend holds that the Danish flag, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flag-of-denmark">Dannebrog</a>, fell from the sky during the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lindanise">Battle of Lindanise</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1312">1312 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">714 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Charles I of Hungary defeats the Aba family at Rozgony</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary">Charles I of Hungary</a> defeated the sons of the late Palatine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-aba">Amadeus Aba</a>, backed by troops of Matthew Csák, near Rozgony. The victory ended the Aba family's rule over eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and strengthened Charles against the great oligarchs.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rozgony">Battle of Rozgony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary">Charles I of Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-aba">Amadeus Aba</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1389">1389 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">637 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Serbs and Ottomans fight the Battle of Kosovo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Prince Lazar's Serbian army met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a>'s forces on the Field of Blackbirds; both rulers were killed. The battle weakened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and became central to Serbian national memory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1844">1844 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">182 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Goodyear patents vulcanised rubber</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Goodyear patented his process of heating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> with sulphur so that it stayed firm and elastic in heat and cold. Vulcanised rubber made possible tyres, seals and hoses.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler and Mussolini hold talks in Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At their first meeting, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> was unimpressed by the German leader, and the two clashed over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Within a few years they had drawn together in the Rome-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mount Pinatubo erupts in the Philippines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The second-largest eruption of the twentieth century sent ash 35 km into the sky. Its aerosols cooled global temperatures by about 0.5°C, and timely evacuations saved thousands of lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 15 June <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-the-black-prince.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward the Black Prince</span><span class="tp">1330–1376</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edvard-grieg"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Edvard Grieg</span><span class="tp">1843–1907</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-tombalbaye"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-tombalbaye.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Tombalbaye</span><span class="tp">1918–1975</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/xi-jinping"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/xi-jinping.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Xi Jinping</span><span class="tp">b. 1953</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 15 June <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/romanos-i-lekapenos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/romanos-i-lekapenos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Romanos I Lekapenos</span><span class="tp">c. 870–948</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoshitsune"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/minamoto-no-yoshitsune.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Minamoto no Yoshitsune</span><span class="tp">1159–1189</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andronikos-iii-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andronikos-iii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andronikos III Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">1297–1341</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-vi-kantakouzenos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John VI Kantakouzenos</span><span class="tp">c. 1292–1383</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lazar-of-serbia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lazar-of-serbia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lazar of Serbia</span><span class="tp">c. 1329–1389</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-duke-of-berry"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-duke-of-berry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John, Duke of Berry</span><span class="tp">1340–1416</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-the-good.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip the Good</span><span class="tp">1396–1467</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/w-arthur-lewis"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">W. Arthur Lewis</span><span class="tp">1915–1991</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
